# Build output. `.next-*/` does not match `.next/` — the glob needs the dash —
# so both are listed. A production build is dropped into `.next-verify/` by
# `npm run verify-demo:build`, which is why the wildcard exists at all.
.next
.next-*/
test-results/
playwright-report/
node_modules

# Generated. `--check/` is a marketing export somebody produced by running
# `scripts/export-marketing.ts --check`, where the script read the flag as its
# output path. It is 59 tracked files nothing should read — and a directory
# whose name starts with `--` is a live hazard for a tool invoked as
# `prettier --check`, so it is excluded rather than left to be shell-expanded
# into an argument.
--check/

# Lockfiles. Rewriting one to satisfy a formatter is how a lockfile stops
# matching what the package manager would produce.
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Agent worktrees. `.git/info/exclude` keeps these out of git's view, but that
# file is local and uncommitted, so every other tool in the repo still walks
# into them. This has twice made a gate report errors in files nobody here
# wrote — once in ESLint, once in the API repo's own `format:check`.
.claude
